# Cloudflare/Netlify `_headers`. Nitro appends its own generated rules below
# this file's contents, so the /assets/* immutable cache rule still applies.
#
# NOT the resume protection. This rule is defense-in-depth only, and it is a
# silent no-op on any other target: under the Vercel preset this whole file is
# copied to .vercel/output/static/_headers and served as a public file at
# /_headers, where nothing reads it. Verified by building with
# NITRO_PRESET=vercel — the generated config.json contained only the /assets/*
# cache rule, with no trace of the line below.
#
# The actual guarantee is "Disallow: /resume.pdf" in public/robots.txt, which is
# copied verbatim into the static output on every preset. If you delete this
# file, nothing is lost; if you delete that line, the phone number in the PDF
# becomes indexable.
#
# Nitro routeRules would be the native fix, but @lovable.dev/vite-tanstack-config
# only forwards preset/output/cloudflare, so they are unreachable from here.
/resume.pdf
  x-robots-tag: noindex
